  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Quiet weather period with warming trend this week.\n\nClouds continue to across the mountains early this evening with\nsome additional cloud cover generally east oF Route 29 in VA/NC.\nBoth areas will experience decreasing cloud cover through the\nevening hours, especially eastern sections. The while there will\nbe a downward trend in coverage across the mountains through the\nnight from east to west. A few flurries/sprinkles still cannot\nbe ruled out over portions of western Greenbrier County through\nthe evening hours. \n\n500mb heights will slowly increase as well and lead to \nprogressively warmer days each day throughout the work week. \nHighs Monday will generally be near average or slightly below \naverage in the 40s/50s across the area, with widespread 60s to \nnear 70 overtaking the area by midweek. While daytime highs will\nwarm up to these temperatures, clear skies and calm winds will \nallow for efficient radiational cooling each night with some \nlows in the 20s and gradually \"warming\" into the 30s.",
